# Ask a robot for its map of one region, with when it observed each cell.
#
# The sending half of a map exchange in stale_map_demo. The reply is the
# robot's whole grid with every cell outside the region set to -1, so that it
# is on the receiver's geometry, and the time, in seconds, at which the robot
# last observed each cell, or at which the robot it took the reading from
# did. An occupancy grid alone cannot say which of two contradicting readings
# is the later; this is what can.

# A region the robot watches, by name. Empty for the whole grid.
string region

---

bool ok
string message
nav_msgs/OccupancyGrid map
float64[] observed

# What the robot's map says of the region: "clear", "blocked" or "unknown".
string verdict
